Package: SVMC
Type: Package
Title: Structural Variant Mapping and Characterization for Bacterial Genomes
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Matthew", "D'Iorio", email = "matthew.diorio@mail.mcgill.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A pipeline and analysis framework for identifying, classifying,
    and validating large-scale structural variation in complete bacterial
    genome assemblies. SVMC orients genomes to the replication origin (OriC)
    using multi-marker scoring, aligns genomes with MUMmer, classifies
    structural variant classes including replication-associated structural
    rearrangements (RASRs), groups recurrent variants into motifs, and
    identifies lineage-defining motifs using a phi-coefficient exclusivity
    score validated against MASH distance clustering.
